tier: frontier
difficulty: 5  # money-path, high blast radius
work_class: money-path
branch: feat/gateway-contract-inject
owns: src/charon/forwarder.py, tests/test_forwarder_contract_inject.py
accept: PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m pytest tests/test_forwarder_contract_inject.py -v -q
  # FAIL-ON-REVERT: (1) flag OFF -> request body is BYTE-IDENTICAL (no injected turn);
  # (2) an exception in the injector -> original body forwarded (fail-OPEN), never a 500;
  # (3) flag ON -> exactly one additive system turn prepended, size-capped, generic text.
prompt: /home/stack/charon-private/prompts/gateway-contract-inject.md   # author at activation
scope: >-
  DEFERRED step-3 of the session-guardrails design (PROPOSAL-SESSION-GUARDRAILS.md; memory
  [charon-gateway-contract-inject-deferred] + [session-guardrails-two-tier]). Inject a generic
  process-discipline "contract" system message into every CG request at forwarder.py:113-123 — the
  only lever that steers opencode/CG sessions BEHAVIORALLY at runtime (native Claude hooks can't reach
  CG). HARDENED build only: flag-guarded, real try/except FAIL-OPEN (the forwarder.py:121 precedent has
  NO try/except), byte-identical when OFF, additive-only (prepend, never rewrite turns), size-capped.
  Contract text generic — NO repo internals/paths/ticket names ([public-repo-no-personal-info]).
  DATA-EGRESS: text ships to third-party providers every call — keep doctrine generic.
  DO-NOT-BUILD-UNTIL: the wake-trigger fires — fleet/cg-drift.sh reports >=2 CG discipline failures in
  30 days (surfaced by preflight detect_cg_drift). Below threshold this stays parked; static-doc
  doctrine (MANAGER-OPERATING-RULES.md, referenced by JOIN-PROMPT + CG AGENTS.md) is the interim.

## Dependencies & sequence
depends_on: (evidence gate) cg-drift.sh trigger >=2/30d — NOT a build dep, a WARRANT dep. Do not
  un-park on speculation; only when preflight's detect_cg_drift goes red.
real-dep: CI required-check + land-push gate must be live first (they are what LOG the drift events
  that arm this trigger). Without them the tally never fills and this correctly stays parked.
concurrency: co-owns forwarder.py with the whole money path -> NOT parallel-safe with meter/drain work.
note: PARKED — deferred by DTC on blast-radius grounds 2026-07-11. Un-park ONLY on the cg-drift trigger.
  ADVERSARIAL review mandatory before merge (money-path, fail-open correctness is where a bug 500s all
  routed traffic).
